## Source audit and change

- Java `Message.getTags()` and `getKeys()` delegate to virtual
  `getProperty(String)`. Rust inherited these methods through `Deref`, which
  called the base `Message` implementation and bypassed
  `MessageExtSubtype::property`.
- Added explicit `MessageExt::tags()` and `keys()` methods that use the
  virtual property hook.
- The invoked Java custom subtype returns `subtype-tag` and `subtype-key` from
  `getProperty`; direct-consume callbacks compare the values and read counts.
  The same fixture continues to compare ProcessQueue's custom `MAX_OFFSET`
  behavior and `msgAccCnt=12`.
- Updated Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 compatibility records and the release
  checklist. Other property-derived getters and inherited methods remain open.

